verses.text:
Once her streets teemed with crowds.{a}
Today the city sits alone, and how quiet she is!{b}
Nations used to look up to her.
Now she is as helpless as a widow.
Provinces once paid her tribute.
Now she herself is made to serve.

The Lord was so angry that He covered Zion’s daughter with a dark cloud.{a}
He threw Israel’s glory down from heaven to the ground.
On the day of His anger He forgot His own footstool.{b}

In burning anger He cut off every strong horn of Israel.{c}
He pulled back His right hand when the enemy came.
He burned in Jacob like a fire that eats everything around it.
